<title>INDIA: Indian soybean prices improve on good plant demand.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean prices improve on good plant demand.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian soybean prices on Friday improved on good plant demand at lower levels with prices up by 100-150 rupees per tonne, dealers said.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices remained weak in very limited trade. Soyoil refined fell by 300 rupees but soyoil solvent was steady on easy undertone.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices were down on limited export demand against better offerings from sellers. Soymeal yellow was $258-260 per tonne for spot and November shipment in exports. Rapeseed extraction was $116-117 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction was 4,000 rupees FOR (Free on Rail) Bedibunder and was 3,950-3,975 rupees FOR (Free on Rail) Bhavnagar.</p>
